      <!-- ASSESSMENT AND PLAN SECTION -->
      <component>
        <section>
          <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9"/>
          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" codeSystemName="LOINC" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>1. Essential Hypertension (I10): Well controlled on Lisinopril 20mg daily. Continue current regimen.
2. Atypical Chest Pain (R07.9): 12-lead EKG performed in office (CPT 93000) showing normal sinus rhythm without acute ischemic changes. Low cardiac risk profile. Advised on lifestyle modifications and return precautions.</text>
        </section>
      </component>

      <!-- PROGRESS NOTE & MEDICAL NECESSITY EVALUATION SECTION -->
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="11506-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" codeSystemName="LOINC" displayName="Progress note"/>
          <title>Clinical Progress Note &amp; Medical Necessity Evaluation</title>
          <text>CLINICAL EVALUATION &amp; MEDICAL NECESSITY JUSTIFICATION:
Patient John Doe (DOB 04/12/1975) was evaluated on 2026-08-10 at Metropolitan Medical Center for medical management of essential hypertension and new-onset atypical chest discomfort. 
Detailed clinical assessment justifies the medical necessity of comprehensive Evaluation &amp; Management (CPT 99214) due to moderate-to-high medical decision making complexity and multi-system chronic disease management. 
In-office 12-lead diagnostic electrocardiogram (CPT 93000) was medically necessary to rule out acute coronary syndrome and evaluate for hypertensive cardiovascular changes. 
Adherence to Lisinopril 20mg daily was verified with patient showing favorable hemodynamic stability.
All diagnostic and therapeutic services rendered meet established clinical guidelines and coverage criteria for claim reimbursement under reference CLM-2026-98124.</text>
        </section>
      </component>
